A||||5||polomeno||Where is tach filter on a 4 cyl??||||1||
Z||000000||polomeno||11-26-2000||06:37 PM||||Hey guys i can't seem to find where the tach filter is on my 4 cylinder 84 .. i know what it looks like but cant' find it.. does anyone happen to have a pic of one on the engine?? or anything that would help.. <P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||11-26-2000||07:16 PM||||My 1986 Helm's manual says it's, "Taped to engine harness, LH end of engine."  Then it sends you to look at a cartoon, which seems to show the tach filter mounted on a stud sticking up from the head, near the forward LH corner of the valve cover.  Might say the "north by northwest corner" of valve cover  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">.<P>Looks like that same stud has the tach filter, a ground wire, and a tube bracket piled on it.  Then a nut on top of all that.<P>Hopefully, 1984 Fieros are the same.  Hope this helps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||polomeno||11-26-2000||10:47 PM||||hmm i just spent like half an hour lookin at my engine and couldnt find anything... does anyone have a 84 and have a pic or some directions to find this damn thing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>thanks<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierose||11-27-2000||03:10 PM||||If you know what it looks like and can't find it then I would say most likely it was removed at some point in time.  There's two wires coming out of it cylindrical in shape.  Mounted on a bracket that's around the fuel filter at least on an 85.  If your tach doesn't work then it's probably gone.  On the forum it's been said that sometimes a bad tach filter can cause problems so people sometimes disconnect remove them.  That's what I did until I buy/make a new one.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||polomeno||11-27-2000||03:13 PM||||that could be it then... cause i see nothign near the fuel filter that looks remotly like it.. now i need to find the wires that i would use to reconnect it...||||reg||1
